:: route_d

—(If the player went on a Garp route during the previous work day:)--- 

{$garp}: Oh, that reminds me! Thanks for doing what you did earlier. You really helped us all out!

—(If the player did not go on a Garp route during the previous work day:)--- 

{$garp}: Oh, that reminds me! The others told me about how you helped them out. Nice work.

Both options, continue

{$name}: Oh, it was no big deal! I’m glad I could help!

{$garp}: It’s clear that you’ve got a good head on your shoulders. Makes sense why Tsuru took such a shine to you.

{$garp}: Anyway, that’s enough talking. Eat up! What’s your favorite kind of food?

Something sweet.
{$garp}: Sweets, huh? I prefer salty stuff myself, but I hear ya. Alright, wait here.
Something salty. (+)
{$garp}: Heh, good to see that SOMEONE has good taste around here! Alright, wait here.
Something savory.
{$garp}: Savory, huh? I prefer salty stuff myself, but I hear ya. Alright, wait here.

{$name}: (Huh? He’s getting up… Wait, why is he going back to the food line?)

{$name}: (...He’s chatting with the server. Well, I guess I should eat…)

…
…
…

{$name}: (Oh, he’s back… and that’s a LOT of food. Oh boy.)

{$garp}: Here you go, [Name]! Eat up! Salty food’s the best, but I tried to get things you’d like.

{$name}: (I wouldn’t have minded seconds, but this came out of nowhere. I should…)
(Just refuse. I didn’t ask for this.) (-)
{$name}: Um, no thanks. I’m full. 
{$garp}: …Oh.
{$name}: (...Oh no. Now he’s just staring at me. I’d better go.)
{$name}: Um, see you around, sir!
{$garp}: …Yeah. See you around.
=>end
(Eat what I can, I guess. He went out of his way to get it for me, and I’m not really full yet.)
{$name}: Oh! Thank you!
{$garp}: Heh, best to eat good food while you can!
(Dig in! This stuff’s the best, and I don’t get this every day.) (+)
{$name}: Mmmmm, thish ish delish.
{$garp}: BWAHAHAHA! Finally, a Marine with a stomach like mine!

{$name}: Whew! That was good. I’m surprised they were willing to give you extra, though… They’ve never let me get seconds before. 

{$garp}: It’s just because you haven’t spent enough time talking to them! They work hard, but they’re often underappreciated. Whenever I take the time to thank them or compliment their cooking, it makes ‘em just a little prouder, a little more motivated to do what they’re good at. 

{$garp}: It takes all sorts to make the Navy work, [Name]. There’s heroes, sure, and you can be one if you really want to. You can be just about anything if you put in the effort and have a good bit of luck. But the chefs? The mechanics? The people who supervise the den-den mushi? The chore boys who start as janitors? They’re incredibly important. When you’ve been in the Marines for as long as I have, you learn to appreciate all the people who work with you to make you who and what you are.
Wow… that’s really admirable. Makes the work I do feel that much more important, honestly. (+)
{$garp}: Of course it’s important. The work that Tsuru does and that you’re helping her with? It’s absolutely necessary… I guess.
Huh, I’ve never really thought about it before. (-)
{$garp}: Hm. Well, it’s worth thinking about. Don’t take people for granted.
Hmm, I don’t know about that… It definitely feels like some people are more important than others, and not just in terms of rank. 
{$garp}: As much as I want to say you’re wrong, I understand why it may feel that way. 

{$garp}: I know heroes get much more news attention and they’re used for propaganda. Maybe it’s hypocritical coming from me, but I still think that everyone who supports those heroes need to be recognized as well; otherwise, the Marines would fall apart. 

{$garp}: …That said, heroes don’t always wear Marine uniforms either. 

{$name}: (Wait, what was that last bit? I couldn’t quite make out his mumbling…)

{$garp}: Anyway, speaking of support, who do you think is the most important person on a ship, other than the captain?

{$name}: (Huh, now there’s a change of subject. Well, let’s see…)
The first mate.
{$garp}: Bwahahaha! Alright, I’ll give you that one. Not quite, though.
The doctor.
{$garp}: Certainly not a bad answer! Not what I was thinking of, though.
The chef. (+)
{$garp}: Got it in one!

{$garp}: At sea, the chef is the second most important person aboard a ship. They have to plan meals, supervise ingredients and rations, and be able to juggle everyone’s food preferences and necessities. Their skills range from perfectly crisping rice crackers to making sure there’s enough vitamins in everyone’s diets. Our lives are in their hands. And a skilled chef can work with just about anything!

{$garp}: I’ve eaten Sea Kings before, and if not for my chef, some of them would be downright disgusting. Have you ever eaten a Sea King, [Name]?
No, I’ve never had the chance. I’d love to try one, though! (+)
{$garp}: An adventurous eater, huh? Good for you! Maybe one day you’ll get lucky!
Are you kidding me?! Of course not! (-)
{$garp}: Hmph, too bad. I didn’t take you for the picky type.
Only once. It was… an experience.
{$garp}: Heh, I’m not surprised. Sea Kings ain’t your average, everyday meal!

{$garp}: Each one’s got a real unique flavor. Sea Kings from the Blues are smaller and more tender than those from the Grand Line—they’re really good when they’re crispy—but Grand Liners are huge! That said, it’s the fishmen who know how to cook ‘em up just right. Go to Fishman Island, and you’ll have a feast you’ll never forget!

{$name}: 
Wow! Do you have history with the fishman, Gar… sir? (+)
=>route_e
Eurgh, fishmen? Are you serious? (-)
=>route_f
Wha—keep your voice down! Someone’s going to hear!
=>route_g

:: route_e

{$garp}: Bwahaha! Sure I do! Humans are quick to point fingers, but the fishmen are a good lot. They’ve suffered too much at the hands of humans, and yet they still manage to maintain good relations with some of them. Of course, there have been times when I’ve fought against fishmen too, but… well, I think that most people are intimidated by them based on appearances, but they’re some of the most stalwart warriors of the sea you’ll ever meet.
Huh… I’ve never actually met one before. They sound interesting. (+)
{$garp}: “Interesting” is one way to put it! If you can, try to get to know more about them. The world feels that much bigger once you realize that humans aren’t the only “people” out there.
Honestly, I’m surprised. I’ve only ever heard rumors, and most of them aren’t so nice.
{$garp}: …It’s complicated. Let’s just say that fishmen and the nobles of the world, including the Celestial Dragons, have a real difficult history, and that’s reflected in what the everyday folk tend to hear. But if you mean what you say about protecting people, just think about what your definition of “people” is.
I thought that the fishmen were either slaves or enemies… (-)
{$garp}: …Nah, [Name]. They’re people. They may not be human, but there’s way more than humans out there in the world. The sooner humans start realizing that, the better.

{$name}: (“People,” huh…)
As far as I’m concerned, the only people I really need to worry about are humans. (-)
{$garp}: You think so, huh?
=>route_f
You say that, but I’m not sure that the rest of the Navy agrees with you.
{$garp}: …You might be right. But I have to believe that times are changing, and that humans’ tyranny over others will come to an end.
{$name}: (...If it were anyone else, they’d probably be arrested for treason. I’m amazed that he can say all that.)
=>route_g
I’ve only ever seen other humans, but I’d love to meet fishmen and all the other people of the seas one day. (+)
{$garp}: That’s a good attitude, [Name]. It’s that kind of thinking that will change the future for the better.
{$garp}: Some of us have had bad experiences with fishmen and people of other races before, but… just like you can’t judge humanity by the actions of one person, people of other races deserve the same courtesy.
=>route_h
:: route_f

{$garp}: …

{$garp}: Here’s the thing, [Name]. You’ll find many Marines who agree with you. But I’m not one of them.

{$garp}: When you said that you wanted to protect people, you only meant humans, didn’t you? I get it. Everyone who’s not human is soooooooo big and scary. They have weird powers and they don’t listen to our laws and they’re just too different. That’s the argument, isn’t it? That humans need to be protected from them?

{$name}: (Oh no. Everyone’s staring…)

{$garp}: Well, I don’t agree. Some of the finest people I know aren’t Marines at all, and some of the worst scum of the seas wear the whites. If we don’t work together alongside the other people of the seas, humans will suffer for it. Hell, we already are!

{$name}: Garp, I—

{$garp}: Sorry, [Name]. I’ve suddenly lost my appetite. I’ll see you around. (-)(-)

{$name}: …

=>end

:: route_g

{$garp}: Bwahahaha! You’re looking at me like I’m about to disappear! What are they gonna do to me, [Name]?

{$garp}: I’m more useful to the higher-ups as a public figure. Whatever I say, they can play it off. So long as I'm still here, I can still try to help the next generation of Marines down the right path. 

{$garp}: Tsuru… Senny… they mean the world to me. But they’re not willing to speak up when it matters. They’re not willing to say the terrible truth out loud. They know I’m right, but they risk damaging everything we’ve fought to build and protect if either of them so much as nod.

{$garp}: …

{$garp}: I’d like to think that I’ve tried to do the right thing. I haven’t always succeeded—hell, I haven’t even succeeded when it mattered most. But even so, if I close my eyes to it all, then what kind of example am I for the younger generation who’s giving it all they’ve got? I’d just be failing you all miserably if I did that. 

{$name}: …
I guess Tsuru and Sengoku are more concerned about appearances than what’s right.
{$garp}: It’s not that they don’t care about what’s right, but they have too much to lose. 
{$name}: And you don’t?
{$garp}: …With one or two exceptions, I’ve already lost the things that matter most to me. All I can do now is protect what I have left.
=>route_h
If the higher-ups are hiding things from us, then I’m not sure that I really want to know. (-)
{$garp}: …Well, that’s your choice.
=>route_h
Thank you for that. (+)
{$garp}: If even one Marine is able to make the world better because of what I’ve taught them, then it’ll all have been worth it.
=>route_h
	

:: route_h

{$garp}: Anyway, I got real sidetracked, huh? We were talking about cooking! I’m starting to get hungry…

{$name}: (Oh, right! I almost forgot that’s where this all started.)

{$name}: Well, I guess I know a thing or two about good food. See, my mom’s really good at baking. I used to watch her in the kitchen, and I’d even help her out sometimes! I was her best taste-tester.

{$garp}: Oh yeah? How about you, then? Did you pick up her talent for cooking?

{$name}: Well…
Not to brag, but I’d call myself better than average. (+)
{$garp}: Bwahahaha! Alright, let’s see you prove it!
=>route_i
A little bit, yeah!
{$garp}: Oh yeah? Gotta say, I’m pretty curious!
=>route_i
Unfortunately, no. 
{$garp}: Well, that’s too bad, but you can’t do it all.
=>route_j
Only if you like your food crispy. EXTRA crispy. (+)
{$garp}: Bwahahaha! Now that’s a taste I’m pretty used to.
=>route_j

:: route_i

{$garp}: Let’s see you put your money where your mouth is! Why don’t you cook something for me, [Name]? I’d love to see your skills!

{$name}: Putting me on the spot, huh?
Fine, I accept your challenge! (+)
{$garp}: Bwahahaha! Excellent! Let’s head back to the kitchens…
=>game_sequence1
Not happening! (-)
{$garp}: …Well, that’s disappointing. Never took you as one to back down from a challenge, but maybe I misjudged you. 
Hold it! There’s no way I’m backing down now!
{$garp}: Heh, that’s what I’m talking about! The kitchens are that way…
=>game_sequence1
I don’t care what you say; I’m not cooking right now, and that’s final! (-)
{$garp}: Hmph, have it your way. You should probably get back to work then, [Name].
=>end

