:: right_order

{$garp}: Bwahahaha! These are delicious, [Name]! You really did a good job.

{$garp}: …

{$garp}: Way back when, I had to catch and cook my own food. Usually just ate meat until I was sick of it. But when I joined the Marines, I really learned how to appreciate all kinds of food. Hell, if you can believe it, Tsuru was the one who introduced me to rice crackers in the first place. 

{$garp}: I was a new recruit, and I had trouble fitting in. I was too powerful, too loud, too… much for a lot of people to handle. I got used to being alone and acting alone. But one day, when I was sitting by myself, Tsuru came over, introduced herself, and thrust a bag of rice crackers into my hand. 

{$garp}: …They were the best thing I’d eaten in a long time.

{$garp}: That’s why food’s so important to me, [Name]. It brings people together. When people eat together, they get to talk to each other. Learn from each other. Bond. And it’s because of Tsuru’s kindness that I made irreplaceable friends and comrades. But now that I’ve become a “Marine legend,” nobody other than the people who knew me from way back when or my crew dare to sit with me anymore. 

{$garp}: It made me truly happy that you sat with me. Thank you, [Name].

{$name}: Anytime! I’d love to sit and eat with you again, Garp… uh, sir.

{$garp}: BWAHAHAHAHA! For you, [Name], Garp is just fine.
=> date_end1

:: wrong_order

{$garp}: Well, you tried your best. Don’t worry too much about it; I’m not that great at cooking either!
Look, it was just a fluke! (-)
{$garp}: Hey now, don’t get riled up over it. Mistakes happen, especially in the kitchen. Just means you’ve still got a ways to go.
Yeahhhh, I’ve still got a lot to learn, I guess. (+)
{$garp}: Don’t sell yourself short; you did your best, and that’s good enough for me!
Somehow, that doesn’t surprise me. 
{$garp}: Bwahahaha! You’ve got me all figured out, huh?

{$garp}: Way back when, I used to kill animals and roast meat over a fire. Toughened me up so I could handle whatever the seas threw at me. Taught my grandkids the same way, and even now, Luffy, my youngest, still loves meat the most. 

{$garp}: …

{$garp}: Heh, you’re awfully easy to talk to, [Name]. It’s been a while since I’ve opened up to someone else this much. 

{$name}: I like talking to you too! I didn’t know you had grandkids, though. Or… well, I knew that Strawhat Luffy was your grandson, but…

{$garp}: Bwahahaha! Maybe I’ll tell you about them some other time.
=> date_end1

:: date_end1

{$garp}: Alright, [Name], I’m sure Tsuru’s missing you by now. 

3 right:

Thanks for the great meal, [Name]. You clearly know what you’re doing in the kitchen, so if you ever get bored of getting paper cuts, just let me know! I’d love to eat a meal of yours again! (+)(+)
=> end

2 right:

That wasn’t too shabby, [Name]! Thanks for the treat. Let me know if you’re up for cooking something again or if you just want to grab a meal—either one’s fine with me. (+)
=> end

1 right:

Keep practicing your cooking, and maybe next time you’ll finish strong. Still, that was pretty fun! Come sit with me again some time!
=> end

None right:

Eh, the crackers didn’t turn out that great, but the company was nice. Go ahead and get back; I’ll be around soon. I’m still pretty hungry, and those rice crackers weren’t exactly edible… (-)
=> end

:: route_j

{$garp}: Don’t worry too much about whether you’re a good cook or not. Nobody can do it all, you know.

{$garp}: Take my crew, for example: Bogard worries about all the shit I can’t be bothered to remember. Burg, my chef, is the best there is. Silia, my doctor, can spot exhaustion with just a look. Harper, my quartermaster, keeps inventory down to the smallest crumb. And then there’s Koby, who has become a hero for the next generation in a way I never could… 

{$garp}: You have a crew because they do all the things that you can’t do. And since nobody can do it all, it’s nice knowing I have a whole ship of fools still willing to sail with me after all this time.

{$name}: Wow. Honestly…
I’m surprised that you can admit to that. (-)
{$garp}: What do you take me for, a stuck-up Admiral who can’t appreciate his subordinates?
I’m glad! If you could actually do everything, then I think you wouldn't be this easy to talk to.
{$garp}: I’m glad you think so. I wish more people thought of me that way; my strength is also a weakness.
I’d really like to surround myself with people like that too. (+)
{$garp}: Knowing you, you’ll get there. You’re real good at making people like you, and that’s a strength if I’ve ever seen one!

{$garp}: Good Marines embrace their own strengths and weaknesses. Sometimes you work to compensate for your weaknesses, like learning what’s edible, but other times you focus on your strengths because other people will cover the rest. That’s what it means to be on a team, and to have a crew. It’s why specialists matter.

{$garp}: …I’m sure you know by now that my grandson, Strawhat Luffy, has been going around collecting all sorts of weirdos from around the seas. I’ve met some of them and they’re good people. They make up for what he lacks and he rewards them by loving them fiercely. It’s no wonder they’re all so joyful despite being wanted by the law. Like me, that boy can’t cook to save his life, but at least he has people who’ll look out for him.

{$garp}: Of course, that’s not to say that you shouldn’t compensate for your weaknesses. Your life is your own, and you’ve gotta decide what’s best for you.
I think I’d rather focus on my strengths and have a team to support me. (+)
{$garp}: Heh, a Marine after my own heart! It means you’ll have to be responsible for covering their weaknesses too, but that’s what a crew does.
I think I’d rather cover my weaknesses just enough that they won’t slow me down.
{$garp}: Fair enough! It’s not a bad thing to work on things you’re bad at. You might never be good at them, but at least it won’t be a detriment!
I think I’d like to be a jack of all trades and be decent at everything. 
{$garp}: You can certainly try, and many people have. It’s a difficult road, but if that’s your calling, then go for it with all you’ve got! 

{$garp}: …

{$garp}: …You know, you’re awfully easy to talk to, [Name]. It’s been a while since I’ve opened up to someone else this much. 
I just like getting to know you better!
{$garp}: Oh yeah? Guess I’m not as much of a boring old fogey as I thought.
I feel the same way. I’ve enjoyed chatting with you. (+)
{$garp}: I’m glad you think so. You’re a real interesting one.
Don’t worry; I’m not usually the type to hold conversations like this either. (-)
{$garp}: Well, it’s not like I’ve been closing myself off because I want to…

{$garp}: Anyway, as much as I’d love to keep you, I’m sure you’ve gotta get back to Tsuru.
Yeah, I should get back to work… (-)
{$garp}: …Yeah. See you around, [Name].
=>end
I guess so. Think we could eat together again soon? (+)
{$garp}: Bwahahaha! Any time you want, [Name]!
=>end
I should… but maybe I’ll ask her about cooking classes too!
{$garp}: Bwahahaha! Then in that case, I’ll look forward to the day you’ll cook for me, [Name]!
=>end

